# The Proxmox reaper.
#
# Install on a cluster node, not the Mac. Two reasons: it keeps running while
# the Mac is asleep, and it needs `pct` to check a guest for the done sentinel,
# which cannot be done over the API.
#
#   scp k8s/proxmox-reaper.cron root@pve1:/etc/cron.d/ccvm-reaper
#   scp dist/ccvm-linux-amd64 root@pve1:/usr/local/bin/ccvm
#
# The node needs the same CCVM_PROXMOX_* settings a workstation uses; put them
# in /etc/ccvm/environment, which this reads.
#
# Every two minutes: on proxmox the reaper is what acts on ccvm-done, so an
# hourly schedule would make ending a session from inside appear broken.
*/2 * * * * root [ -f /etc/ccvm/environment ] && . /etc/ccvm/environment; /usr/local/bin/ccvm gc >> /var/log/ccvm-gc.log 2>&1
